From 223f98dfd00604f68483a2445213865035823b45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: eval-fork <eval-fork@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:21:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] DR4 completed: owner rule inside the PDP; request
 address on document reads

Owner rule. The owner rule is now the rule P_own of the PDP chain instead of a
constant allow in the PEP gate. It follows P_ctx and P1, is confined to the
owner's department, covers the actions the file endpoints serve (read,
download), and is exempt from P_class like the director and division-manager
rules (the developer guide gives the owner rule priority: Admin -> Owner -> ...).
P_own is placed after P3, so directors and managers keep their rule labels. The
gate, the admin tester and the resource listing no longer decide for owners
themselves, and published documents no longer have an owner shortcut before the
PDP. The integration test for owner decision logging now checks the PDP's
decision row.

Request context. A middleware stores the client address of each request in a
context variable; the document read procedure passes it to the risk helper and
to the PDP, so the ip_change signal of P_ctx is evaluated on document reads as
on the file endpoints. Internal (collaboration-server) calls keep the address
unknown.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
